\details{
\strong{robots.txt ruling.} \code{www.nationalleague.ch/robots.txt} disallows \verb{/api}. The owner approved building on it
on 2026-10-12, for polite, incremental use only: requests are spaced at least one second apart (on every
attempt, retries included), and a bulk backfill or a published mirror needs the owner's sign-off first. Crawl
incrementally: fetch a finished game once (keyed by \code{game_id}), find new games with one \code{\link[=nl_schedule]{nl_schedule()}} call
per run, and fetch season tables at most once per game day.

Seasons are END years and go on the wire unchanged. Ids (\verb{*_id}) are whole-number \code{numeric} (a 14-digit
\code{game_id} exceeds R's 32-bit integer); every other whole-number column is \code{integer}. The club backend key the
API ships in \verb{/teams/\{id\}/info} is dropped before parsing and never returned.

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://www.nationalleague.ch/api/player/\{playerId\}}.
}
\section{Errors}{

Raises a classed condition (all inherit \code{fastRhockey_error}): \code{fastRhockey_no_data} for a 404 or an empty answer (no
games or rows for that season, team or phase), \code{fastRhockey_asset_fetch} for a failed fetch, an error object in a 200, a body
without the ids it must carry, or an answer for another season, team, game or player, and \code{fastRhockey_bad_request}
for a 400/422 or an argument that is not a whole number.
}

